<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Bonnie Blue Flag</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a> (first sung in Jackson, Mississippi, spring <a href="/years/1861">1861</a>; published in New Orleans, <a href="/years/1861">1861</a>)</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonnie-blue-flag">Bonnie Blue Flag</a>&quot;, also known as &quot;We Are a Band of Brothers&quot;, is a marching song of 1861 associated with the Confederate States of America. The entertainer Harry McCarthy wrote the words and set them to the melody of &quot;The Irish Jaunting Car&quot;. The title refers to the Bonnie Blue Flag, the unofficial first flag of the Confederacy.</p></div>
